Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/content/res/AssetManager.java at android-15.0.0_r1
(Apache-2.0), ADR-0039 b3.3 (b3.4's patch brought forward): the system path opens framework-res's folder and asks
for no overlay idmaps.

Why: every AssetManager an app gets goes through createSystemAssetsInZygoteLocked (getSystem(), the public
constructor and AssetManager.Builder; setApkAssets needs the system set it makes). AOSP's version
  - opens /system/framework/framework-res.apk, while Minato ships framework-res as the folder
    /system/framework/framework-res (ADR-0039 decision 8), which ApkAssets.loadFromDir opens; and
  - asks OverlayConfig.getZygoteInstance() for the framework's immutable overlay idmaps, which scans the overlay
    partitions and runs idmap2. Minato has no overlay partitions, so there are no RROs and no idmaps, and
    OverlayConfig is not in framework.jar.
The patch keeps FRAMEWORK_APK_PATH and the method's signature: the folder is the given path without ".apk", and the
idmap list is empty.

tools/build-framework.sh applies it to a copy in build/framework/src, never to build/sources. tools/framework-check.sh
checks that framework.jar's AssetManager is the patched one; tools/asset-manager-check.sh reads framework-res
through it.

--- a/core/java/android/content/res/AssetManager.java
+++ b/core/java/android/content/res/AssetManager.java
@@ -258,10 +258,13 @@
 
         try {
             final ArrayList<ApkAssets> apkAssets = new ArrayList<>();
-            apkAssets.add(ApkAssets.loadFromPath(frameworkPath, ApkAssets.PROPERTY_SYSTEM));
+            // Minato: framework-res ships as the folder of the APK's path without ".apk" (ADR-0039 decision 8).
+            final String frameworkDir = frameworkPath.endsWith(".apk")
+                    ? frameworkPath.substring(0, frameworkPath.length() - ".apk".length()) : frameworkPath;
+            apkAssets.add(ApkAssets.loadFromDir(frameworkDir, ApkAssets.PROPERTY_SYSTEM, null));
 
-            final String[] systemIdmapPaths =
-                    OverlayConfig.getZygoteInstance().createImmutableFrameworkIdmapsInZygote();
+            // Minato has no overlay partitions, so there are no RROs and no idmaps.
+            final String[] systemIdmapPaths = new String[0];
             for (String idmapPath : systemIdmapPaths) {
                 apkAssets.add(ApkAssets.loadOverlayFromPath(idmapPath, ApkAssets.PROPERTY_SYSTEM));
             }
